"Indian urban centers lack adequate wastewater treatment, causing groundwater contamination and coastal pollution. Water scarcity worsens with declining per capita renewable freshwater (from 5,177 to 1,588 m\u00b3 since 1951). Supply falls short (69 vs 135 lpcd), with intermittent access (2\u20133 hours). Untreated sewage remains the largest land-based pollution source for coastal areas. (48 words)"